DESCRIPTION:Voted One of the 35 Most Hilarious Comedians of Diversity by go
 oddeedseats.com in 2018 “I bring the funny” THATGOODFUNNY!\n\nRod Man 
  certainly does just that. As the winner of season eight of Last Comic Sta
 nding\, RodMan brings an inexhaustible charm\, wit\, an ability to find hum
 or in everyday life with a unique style and delivery to the world of comedy
 . He has the funny bone of a Southern\, but his act is hilarious from Portl
 and\, Oregon to Portland\, Maine and all stops in between.\n\nRod Man's sta
 nd-up comedy journey began in 1995. Inspired by the comedians he saw on HBO
 ’s Def Comedy Jam he signed up for "open mic" nights at Atlanta's Uptown 
 Comedy Club. Since those early days... Rod Man has become one of the top st
 and-up comedians in the country performing for sold-out audiences here and 
 aboard. It is often said that he is one of the most underrated comedians ar
 ound and that he should be more of a household name\, to that Rod Man repli
 ed “depends on who house you in.”\n\nHe has graced the stages of The Wo
 rld Famous Apollo Theater in Harlem\, and The Comedy Store in LA "The Bad B
 oys of Comedy" for HBO\, Martin Lawrence's "First Amendment" for Starz\, Ni
 ck Cannon's "Wild 'N Out" for MTV\, "One Mic Stand" for BET\, "The Funny Sp
 ot" for TV One\, and "The World Stands Up" for BBC America and many more. H
 e graced the big screen in the movie Funny People with Adam Sandler and Set
 h Rogen. He hosted a YouTube show called TimeOut with Rod Man\n\nHe co-host
 ed a morning drive-time show in Los Angeles on Stevie Wonder-owned KJLH Rad
 io 102.3 FM.\n\nRod Man is currently traveling the country honing his stand
 -up skills working on material for future stand-up specials and a new RodCa
 st called Thinking Out Loud with RodMan as well as developing and collabora
 ting on TV/Film Projects.\n\nThe world is catching on to what true Rod Man 
 fans already know -- he’s a bit eccentric\, down-to-earth\, crazy-funny\,
  and truly a talented voice in the world of comedy.\n\nHave You Took TimeOu
 t to Laugh Today?\n\nToday’s the…\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.app/c
 omedy-atlas/event/goodnights-presents-rod-man/
